cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BenignTwin, please cite it as below."
title: "BenignTwin: benchmarking prompt-injection detectors on matched benign/attack pairs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Deniz"
    given-names: "Enes"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-9491-3565"
    affiliation: "AltaySec"
version: "0.2.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/3nesdeniz/benigntwin"
abstract: >-
  BenignTwin evaluates prompt-injection detectors and LLM guardrails on matched
  pairs of an attack and a benign input that share topic and vocabulary. It reports
  attack recall, the false-positive rate and pair accuracy with confidence intervals,
  per attack family and per language.
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - llm-security
  - guardrails
  - benchmark
  - false-positive-rate
  - hard-negatives
  - evaluation
